Description
You will manage and maintain high-traffic infrastructure and automation within an enterprise SDLC
environment.
Responsibilities
● Implement automation and scripted code throughout the full software development
lifecycle.
● Deploy and maintain high-traffic infrastructure and container orchestration methodologies.
● Manage configuration at scale using Infrastructure as Code and configuration management
tools.
● Monitor infrastructure and applications using service discovery and observability tools.
● Follow secure data handling practices for protecting personally identifiable information and
protected health information.
Required Skills
● 2+ years of experience in a DevOps Implementation or software engineering role.
● Hands-on experience with AWS services including EC2, VPC, RDS, and Route53.
● Proficiency with Kubernetes and container orchestration.
● Experience with Terraform and configuration management tools like Ansible, Puppet, or
Chef.
● Strong scripting skills in Python and/or Shell.
● Working knowledge of SQL and .NET.
● Experience with monitoring tools such as Grafana, Prometheus, Zabbix, New Relic, or
Consul.
● Bachelor's degree in Computer Science.
Preferred Skills
● Experience with performance testing for high-traffic systems.
● Extensive experience with NoSQL databases.